  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR is test-only. It traces a setup's own machine and post from the pick to the bytes in the posted files (#1224), on top of the #1206 UI pins already in this PR. No product code changed.\n\nFixture (app): Setup1 follows the document, which mounts **machine A** (the shipped VMC 3-axis) and **post A** (the built-in Fanuc). Setup2 owns **machine B** (the shipped Tormach 770M, a 10000 rpm spindle) and **post B** (Siemens 840D). Each setup cuts its own box: Setup1 has Face1a then Face1b at G54, Setup2 has Face2 at G55. The tests check dialect markers, not only file counts. Fanuc files carry `%`, `O0001 (<machine>)` and `M30`. Siemens files carry `; <machine>`, `N10 G17 G710` and `M2`. Each header names its own machine.\n\n- `crates/app/tests/setup_mount_trace.rs` (new, 6 tests)\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp_setup_mount_trace.rs` (new, 1 test)\n- `crates/app/tests/setup_mounts_post.rs`: two edge tests. One is `#[ignore = \"#1232: ...\"]`.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/setup_mount_pages.rs`: the #1206 two-mount pin now also posts through the shell's own `PostProgramFile` command. It reads both files from disk and checks Fanuc on the VMC and Haas on the tilt head, each holding only its own setup's work.\n- `docs/decisions/1224-setup-mount-trace.md`\n\n## Failing rows (filed, not fixed here)\n\n- **#1232 (P1)**, row 7: a lathe setup's turning operation, posted through the setup's own milling post (Haas), is written as a milling program (`G17`, `T2 M6`, `G43 H2`, `S3000 M3`, facing as `Y` moves at `X0`). It should be refused. Pinned by `an_own_milling_post_on_a_lathe_setup_is_refused_by_name` (ignored).\n- **#1233 (P5)**, the MCP half of row 1: no MCP tool sets a setup's own post, so the MCP leg covers the machine pick only. The post pick is pinned app-side.\n\n## Trace table\n\n| Row | Test (path) | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 Stored | `each_mount_file_is_its_own_post_machine_ops_and_work_offset` (app `setup_mount_trace.rs`, new): the document, Setup1 and Setup2 each hold their own machine and post. UI: `the_setup_machine_page_takes_its_own_machine`, `the_setup_post_page_takes_its_own_post_through_the_picker`, `the_setup_machine_page_picks_its_own_machine_from_the_library` (ui `setup_mount_pages.rs`, #1206). MCP: `a_setups_own_machine_picked_over_mcp_reaches_its_own_posted_file_and_undoes` (app `mcp_setup_mount_trace.rs`, new) and existing `setups_declare_activate_and_post_their_own_word` (app `mcp_setup.rs`) | pass. The MCP post pick has no tool: #1233 |\n| 2 Generated (other setup active) | `each_mount_file_is_its_own_post_machine_ops_and_work_offset` (new: Setup1's operations are generated with Setup2 active, and the reverse). Existing: `an_inactive_setups_op_generates_on_its_own_machine_without_activation` (mill/lathe kind law, `setup_mounts_post.rs`), `two_setups_on_different_machines_are_judged_on_their_own_and_the_ribbon_follows_the_active` (`setup_mount.rs`), `the_z_stroke_cap_reads_the_ops_own_setups_machine_not_the_active_one` (`fixture_route.rs`) | pass |\n| 3 Verified / simulated | New: `a_spindle_limit_is_judged_on_each_ops_own_machine_from_either_active_setup` (12000 rpm refused on machine B only, naming Face2, nothing written) and `a_rotary_index_swing_is_judged_on_each_ops_own_machine` (a work-turning A with no nose height refuses only the ops of the setup that mounts it). Existing: `a_travel_limit_is_judged_on_the_ops_own_machine_only` (`setup_mounts_post.rs`), `the_struck_check_judges_each_op_on_its_own_setups_spindle` (`fixture_ux.rs`), the lathe file's `G50 S12000` from its own machine (`a_mill_and_a_lathe_post_two_files_each_byte_identical_to_posting_it_alone`), workholding rpm per setup (`lathe_workholding_rpm.rs`) | pass |\n| 4 Posted | `each_mount_file_is_its_own_post_machine_ops_and_work_offset` (new): two files `_01_Setup1.nc` and `_02_Setup2.nc`. Each is in its own dialect and names its own machine. Each holds only its own operations in order (Face1a before Face1b) at its own work offset (G54 / G55). The bytes are the same whichever setup is active. UI: `each_setup_picks_its_own_machine_and_post_and_posts_one_file_per_mount` (extended: shell Post command, dialect asserts) | pass |\n| 5 Follow the document | `the_document_mount_moves_only_the_following_setup_and_untick_follows_again` (new): a new document machine and post (Tilt-head 5-axis, Haas) change Setup1's file and leave every byte of Setup2's. Unticking Setup2's own post, then its own machine, makes it follow the document (one file at the end). Each untick is one undo step back to the earlier output | pass |\n| 6 Round trip | `two_mounts_round_trip_byte_identical_and_undo_redo_restores_each_output` (new): save, reopen, post gives byte-identical files. Undo and redo of the machine pick and of the post pick each restore the earlier output. Existing: `a_setups_own_machine_and_post_round_trip_and_undo` (`setup_mount.rs`), `the_script_post_writes_one_file_per_mount` (`setup_mounts_post.rs`) | pass |\n| 7 Edges | `the_same_own_mount_is_one_file_and_half_a_mount_is_two` (new): both setups owning machine B and post B give one file through Siemens for machine B with G54 and G55, as `program_mounts` groups. An own machine with a followed post gives two Fanuc files. The reverse gives one machine in two dialects. `an_own_lathe_post_on_a_mill_setup_is_refused_by_name` (new, `setup_mounts_post.rs`): refused (#1190 door), nothing written. `an_own_milling_post_on_a_lathe_setup_is_refused_by_name` (new, ignored) | **lathe setup + milling post: FAILS, #1232**. The rest pass |\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green on the first run. It ran app `mcp_setup_mount_trace` and `setup_mount_trace` (new suites), `setup_mounts_post::an_own_lathe_post_on_a_mill_setup_is_refused_by_name`, the ui lib unit tests, and ui `boundary`, `boundary_picks` and `theme_files`.\n- Each new test was also run by name: `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test setup_mount_trace` (6 passed), `--test mcp_setup_mount_trace` (1 passed), `--test setup_mounts_post -- an_own_ --include-ignored` (the #1232 pin fails as filed), and `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib -- setup_mount_pages` (4 passed).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test setup_mount_trace --test mcp_setup_mount_trace --test setup_mounts_post -- -D warnings` and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --lib --tests -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- No posted file was run on a real control or a control simulator. The dialect checks are text markers.\n- Nothing was looked at on screen. The UI leg drives clicks headlessly.\n- The single-file post of a lathe document whose document post is a milling dialect was not run. #1232 says it is very likely the same path.\n- A user's own `.cps` as a setup's own post was not traced.\n\nChangelog: none (test-only)\n\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nFork: none (canonical repo); branch not refreshed from main by instruction.\n\nFixes #1224\nRefs #1206\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
